        "original_id": "d8810966-ba19-5935-b31d-5df79821f943",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Castle Hill (Virginia), Monticello, Albemarle County, Virginia, Charlottesville, Southwest Mountains\n- People: Thomas Jefferson\n- Registers: Virginia Landmarks Register, National Register of Historic Places\n- Topics: plantations, historic properties\n\nFacts:\n- Monticello was the primary plantation of Thomas Jefferson, the third President of the United States.\n- Thomas Jefferson began designing and building Monticello at age 26 after inheriting land from his father.\n- Castle Hill is a historic, privately owned 600-acre plantation at the foot of the Southwest Mountains in Albemarle County, Virginia, near Monticello and Charlottesville.\n- Castle Hill is recognized by the Virginia Landmarks Register and the National Register of Historic Places.",
